      },
      "lineNbr": 4875,
      "author": {
        "id": 1069543
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-06-30T15:39:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In that future scenario, wouldn\u0027t we have to add some code to binder to use it? Why not just add binder_user_caps then? As-is, the only way it could be used is either in a memory dump or gdb -- seems unlikely to be useful.",
      "parentUuid": "47cc9025_be8c20d5",
      "revId": "f75be47c0bcfa9d3178e6d2da11b5c5f08e66018",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4575a914_73af4bac",
        "filename": "drivers/android/binder.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 4875,
      "author": {
        "id": 1869395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-06-30T16:34:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I believe the idea is to have userspace binder report this info now, and start using it on the driver as/when needed. You are still correct though, the driver doesn\u0027t actually need to pull this info yet; even if it\u0027s being provided by the binder. So I\u0027ll get rid of `ucaps`.",
      "parentUuid": "d8b9424e_47d5d2a0",
      "revId": "f75be47c0bcfa9d3178e6d2da11b5c5f08e66018",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
